# RLS Security Barrier assertions — verify user predicates cannot
# observe RLS-hidden rows through side-channel functions.
#
# Key: assertions use unique "barrier_qN" markers and explicit
# hidden_leaked=0 counts, not just presence of visible rows.

# Q1: barrier_user sees only their own rows through barrier_spy filter
1|visible-1
2|visible-2

# Q2: CRITICAL — spy log contains only visible rows, zero hidden rows leaked.
# "barrier_q2" marker is globally unique. hidden_leaked=0 proves barrier held.
barrier_q2|2|0

# Q3: Direct SELECT — unique "barrier_q3:" prefix per row
barrier_q3:1:visible-1
barrier_q3:2:visible-2

# Q5: CRITICAL — compound predicate (barrier_spy AND id > 1).
# total_seen=2: spy evaluates on all RLS-visible rows (barrier prevents
# id>1 from being pushed below RLS filter). hidden_leaked=0: no leak.
barrier_q5|2|0
